WEBVTT

01:50.840 --> 01:53.509
The cargo's coming into
the city from the east.

01:53.592 --> 01:56.262
We're taking the whole vehicle.

01:57.096 --> 01:58.931
Haul's two 'n' a half mil.

01:59.014 --> 02:01.725
Pot o' gold with the usual split.

02:03.352 --> 02:07.523
This one's definitely
the biggest job I've ever taken.

02:08.232 --> 02:10.109
Target's a corp, ain't it?

02:10.192 --> 02:12.903
Three guesses which one it is.

02:13.696 --> 02:16.157
Arasaka, of course.

02:16.740 --> 02:19.994
Half a mil a head's nice 'n' all,
but I ain't even sure if it's worth it.

02:20.077 --> 02:23.080
Really think five of us is enough?

02:23.164 --> 02:26.167
Security footprint
on the convoy's peculiarly small.

02:26.750 --> 02:31.505
Arasaka's posted a limited crew to cast
a short shadow, keep a low profile.

02:31.589 --> 02:33.966
We'll strike the metal where it's soft.

02:34.049 --> 02:36.051
I dunno, man…

02:36.135 --> 02:38.179
Let's not overthink this.

02:38.262 --> 02:41.307
Smash, grab, deliver. It's what we do.

02:41.390 --> 02:43.058
Business as usual.

02:43.142 --> 02:45.769
Business as usual my ass.

02:46.437 --> 02:49.565
You think he'll withstand
the cyberskeleton?

02:51.400 --> 02:56.780
Arasaka does. After seeing his chemistry
mesh so well with the Sandevistan.

02:56.864 --> 03:03.329
Tanaka wanted him back in the Academy
so he could test the cyberskeleton on him.

03:03.412 --> 03:07.082
And this girl was trying to
bury that information

03:07.166 --> 03:09.960
so no one would come after him.

03:10.044 --> 03:13.881
That's how I see it.
Frying Tanaka tied up a loose end.

03:14.882 --> 03:19.011
Maine and Dorio were just
collateral damage in her schemes.

03:19.553 --> 03:21.305
That's one way of putting it…

03:21.388 --> 03:24.808
So much carnage for one so petite.

03:24.892 --> 03:28.103
How many did she kill just to save one?

03:35.694 --> 03:40.824
Dove a little deeper and found that
she used to work for Arasaka.

03:40.908 --> 03:43.911
They groomed her
to mine data in the Old Net.

03:44.828 --> 03:48.082
Guess that's how she's been able to
get past Arasaka's ICE.

03:49.708 --> 03:51.001
This is perfect.

03:51.085 --> 03:56.966
What a wonderful surprise.
We can dangle her in front of Arasaka.

03:57.049 --> 04:00.261
Our fast-lane ticket up
the corporate rungs!

04:00.344 --> 04:03.222
Didn't see you as
such a simp corpo-climber.

04:03.305 --> 04:05.224
Is that really so strange?

04:05.307 --> 04:07.601
What are fixers
if not glorified pet owners

04:07.685 --> 04:10.062
who keep their mercenary hounds well fed?

04:10.646 --> 04:15.943
The only way to succeed in Night City
is to get in with the corporations.

04:16.026 --> 04:19.238
I'll require your continued assistance.

04:19.321 --> 04:22.157
Gonna make me keep digging
this hole deeper?

04:22.241 --> 04:25.286
This is a great opportunity
for you as well.

04:25.369 --> 04:29.832
I have corporate amnesty for
the Tanaka incident… But what about you?

04:29.915 --> 04:32.668
You're as slimy as ever.

04:32.751 --> 04:36.005
Let's play nice for old time's sake.

04:36.088 --> 04:42.428
How often do we get to work with Arasaka
and stick it to Militech with one hand?

04:42.511 --> 04:45.306
Arasaka wouldn't object.

04:45.973 --> 04:49.476
I'll negotiate for your immunity
and commission.

04:51.103 --> 04:55.065
Never trust a soul in Night City.

04:55.858 --> 04:58.152
Trusting fools deserve
the hand they're dealt…

05:00.529 --> 05:02.990
Is David a bargaining chip as well?

05:03.073 --> 05:07.369
Naturally. I've conjured a plan.

05:07.453 --> 05:10.456
I'll pitch them both to Arasaka.

05:23.427 --> 05:26.096
What's up with the emergency meeting?

05:27.056 --> 05:31.602
Faraday's come through.
It's our biggest gig yet.

05:32.186 --> 05:37.107
Huge risk, huge return. Turn back now
if you're not ready to face the heat.

05:42.613 --> 05:44.198
I'm counting on you too, Kiwi.

05:44.281 --> 05:45.115
Sure.

05:45.199 --> 05:49.036
Yo, granny and gramps
can bench this round.

05:49.119 --> 05:51.789
Think your little chicken legs'll
reach the pedals?

05:51.872 --> 05:53.332
Kiss my ass.

05:54.208 --> 05:55.501
Give us the brief.

05:56.293 --> 05:58.504
'Saka put on a small,
heavy-duty security squad.

05:58.587 --> 06:03.300
But they'll split. Half'll go after
a diversion squad commissioned by Faraday.

06:05.094 --> 06:06.637
Diversion squad?

06:06.720 --> 06:11.391
A decoy, basically. Though that's probably
not in the brief Faraday gave them.

06:11.475 --> 06:12.518
Oh.

06:12.601 --> 06:14.978
Typical Faraday handiwork.

06:15.062 --> 06:18.023
Of course, there's no way to tell
if we're also a decoy…

06:19.858 --> 06:21.110
Bitch!

06:56.854 --> 07:00.232
Good, good. We've got 'em
nice and split. What's the call?

07:00.315 --> 07:03.944
Main target's off the road.
We've got the high ground.

07:04.027 --> 07:05.863
Put her in gear, Falco!

07:06.572 --> 07:07.447
Alright!

07:07.531 --> 07:08.699
Let's hit it!

07:10.993 --> 07:15.497
Hey, David. Car's all warmed and ready…

07:15.581 --> 07:16.790
David!

07:17.583 --> 07:20.169
Are these all immunosuppressants?

07:20.252 --> 07:25.382
Can you fetch my mom's jacket for me?

07:25.466 --> 07:27.509
We're calling off the gig!

07:27.593 --> 07:31.305
Rebecca… I got a favor to ask…

07:31.388 --> 07:32.890
You better knock it--

07:32.973 --> 07:37.394
Becca, I can't ask anyone else…

07:48.113 --> 07:49.031
Rebecca?

07:49.114 --> 07:52.910
Puppy-dog eyes! Knew I'm
a sucker for the vulnerable, didn't ya?!

07:52.993 --> 07:56.371
Don't use your fucking Sandevistan.
You hear me?

07:56.455 --> 07:57.664
Okay, okay…

08:12.930 --> 08:14.640
One down!

08:14.723 --> 08:17.267
Alright, we're right on the target's ass!

08:17.351 --> 08:18.685
I'll hack into the brake.

08:18.769 --> 08:20.395
Hold on, we got a tail!

08:24.483 --> 08:26.777
Can't even get a peek out there!

08:26.860 --> 08:27.986
Leave it to me!

08:28.070 --> 08:31.740
Hey! Don't use your Sandevistan…

08:40.415 --> 08:42.125
Fucking deaf, that one?!

08:49.091 --> 08:53.637
You're a real piece of work!

08:53.720 --> 08:57.766
Damn you, David!

09:03.355 --> 09:04.815
Everyone good?

09:04.898 --> 09:07.234
Hey 'stache! Do we look good?!

09:07.317 --> 09:08.527
Look.

09:09.486 --> 09:11.113
It's still going?!

09:11.196 --> 09:13.365
ICE is as thick as the armor.
Can't hack it.

09:13.949 --> 09:15.576
Then I'll hit 'em from the front.

09:15.659 --> 09:16.785
Seriously, knock it--

09:17.911 --> 09:20.914
Fucking tired of being ignored!

09:26.044 --> 09:28.463
…on autopilot!

10:10.756 --> 10:14.259
So please.
Sit back, relax, and enjoy the show.

10:16.803 --> 10:17.638
Not good.

10:18.221 --> 10:20.891
-We'd better stop it fast before it falls.
-What?!

10:30.067 --> 10:34.279
Alright… What are ya gonna do, David?

10:34.905 --> 10:37.532
We're right on the edge…

10:37.616 --> 10:39.493
Falco! Pull up closer!

10:39.576 --> 10:41.203
Easier said than done…

10:48.085 --> 10:50.379
What do we do?!

10:50.462 --> 10:52.172
I'll shoot it if you won't!

10:59.721 --> 11:03.767
That's right. Easy does it, David.

11:03.850 --> 11:06.895
No one here to slap sense into you now.

11:07.646 --> 11:09.856
Make a choice.

11:09.940 --> 11:13.610
You're special, remember?

11:24.538 --> 11:25.539
Brake!

11:25.622 --> 11:26.873
Slam on 'em!

12:03.785 --> 12:04.953
No way.

12:05.036 --> 12:06.788
Th-That's how it's done.

12:06.872 --> 12:08.373
Bit my tongue…

12:17.924 --> 12:19.384
How nice.

12:19.968 --> 12:24.764
They send an executive-class AV
to collect a street girl?

12:25.348 --> 12:28.018
You really must be
their precious, lost toy.

12:32.105 --> 12:35.233
Still no response from Lucy?

12:35.317 --> 12:39.154
Ugh. What's one more runner
gonna do for us at this point?

12:39.237 --> 12:41.907
You gonna pay her from your pot?

12:41.990 --> 12:43.408
How's it going over there?

12:43.492 --> 12:46.369
Few more minutes to break the lock.

12:46.453 --> 12:50.540
Is it just me or does it bother you
that this carrier was unmanned?

12:50.624 --> 12:53.126
You sure it's an Arasaka vehicle?

12:53.210 --> 12:56.922
If you're so worried,
just take the cargo and go.

12:57.005 --> 12:59.674
We're all waiting on you.

12:59.758 --> 13:03.929
Quit the yapping and let's go get our car.

13:04.012 --> 13:08.975
Sheesh. Didn't strike me back when
we were going after the carrier,

13:09.059 --> 13:13.355
but we'd be fishes in a barrel
if anyone tried to shoot us out here.

13:13.438 --> 13:19.444
Jesus, old man. Nervous fart like you
doesn't deserve that cowboy 'stache!

13:19.528 --> 13:21.696
You'd go weak in the knees if I shaved.

13:21.780 --> 13:24.032
Ew! Gonna kick it off!

13:24.115 --> 13:28.453
Stop dodging, old man!

13:29.162 --> 13:31.915
Looks like the decoy failed.
We've got company!

13:33.875 --> 13:34.960
What?!

13:43.009 --> 13:44.177
That a Basilisk?

13:44.886 --> 13:46.429
And a missile carrier!

13:46.513 --> 13:47.931
You're shitting me…

13:48.014 --> 13:48.932
Militech!

14:05.240 --> 14:09.077
What the fuck?!
Why're we being steamrolled by Militech?!

14:10.412 --> 14:13.582
Faraday's a Militech-man, ain't he?

14:14.165 --> 14:16.418
The fishiness is really starting to reek!

14:19.879 --> 14:20.755
It's open!

14:20.839 --> 14:22.007
That was quick!

14:22.090 --> 14:24.342
Take cover inside. Hurry!

14:25.135 --> 14:27.012
What in the seven hells is this…?

14:27.095 --> 14:30.849
This is what Faraday paid Maine to find?

14:30.932 --> 14:33.143
So what is it?

14:33.226 --> 14:36.855
A cyberskeleton. Military implant.

14:36.938 --> 14:41.026
Military…
You mean like David's Sandevistan?

14:41.109 --> 14:44.487
From what I hear,
it's a whole different caliber.

14:44.571 --> 14:48.617
Hey. This kid's Sandy ain't
nothing to turn your nose up at either.

14:48.700 --> 14:51.328
First time I'm hearing about this.

14:51.411 --> 14:53.204
Believe me or don't.

14:53.288 --> 15:00.128
Arasaka thinks they can overtake Militech
if this thing hits the market.

15:00.211 --> 15:03.048
But they've kept its development
on the down-low.

15:03.131 --> 15:08.637
Most of its information
was concentrated under Tanaka's wing.

15:08.720 --> 15:12.933
I don't know how,
but Faraday got wind of this,

15:13.016 --> 15:17.395
and promised to leak this tech to
Militech to get himself a nice deal.

15:18.146 --> 15:22.150
Not every day you get to fly
above Night City at your leisure.

15:22.233 --> 15:28.406
It must be a nice change of scenery
from your usual ice-filled baths.

15:28.490 --> 15:33.244
What do you say?
Want to help me make your boy fly?

15:37.791 --> 15:38.625
What?

15:38.708 --> 15:39.918
Incoming call from Lucy.

15:40.001 --> 15:42.837
Now is seriously not the time!

15:49.010 --> 15:51.596
No time. Militech's coming.

15:51.680 --> 15:54.349
How do you know that? Where are you?

15:54.432 --> 15:55.684
They're after me too.

16:16.913 --> 16:17.747
Lucy!

16:17.831 --> 16:18.832
What did she say?

16:18.915 --> 16:22.919
"Use the cyberskeleton
if you want to survive."

16:23.003 --> 16:24.004
The fuck?

16:24.087 --> 16:25.714
She didn't seem herself though.

16:25.797 --> 16:26.756
Sure about that?

16:26.840 --> 16:31.803
Someone's after her too.
I've gotta install it.

16:31.886 --> 16:34.764
Whole truck's a mobile installation unit.

16:35.473 --> 16:38.143
That deck's got the installer all set up.

16:38.226 --> 16:40.437
You are not gonna install this thing!

16:40.520 --> 16:42.105
I gotta get us out of this!

16:42.188 --> 16:46.693
Are you insane?! You don't even know
what this hunk of metal can do!

16:47.277 --> 16:49.779
I don't see any other option.

16:49.863 --> 16:51.948
Besides me knocking you the fuck out?!

16:52.032 --> 16:54.284
I'm gonna go get our car.

16:54.367 --> 16:55.201
I'll go with.

16:55.285 --> 16:56.536
Thanks!

16:56.619 --> 17:01.082
Last time I installed something that
wasn't mine, Maine beat the shit outta me.

17:02.542 --> 17:04.210
Some things just don't change!

17:04.294 --> 17:08.131
Don't! Wait…

17:10.925 --> 17:14.471
You fucking gonk!
Why don't you ever listen?!

17:21.978 --> 17:25.231
What's Militech waiting for?

17:25.315 --> 17:27.734
Kiwi, you able to get eyes on…

17:29.319 --> 17:30.820
Sorry.

17:44.417 --> 17:45.543
What?!

18:17.784 --> 18:20.954
Did you truly think
we would put no failsafe in place?

18:38.847 --> 18:42.600
Shall I open a second neural port
in the back of your skull?

18:45.061 --> 18:48.106
-I'm afraid she's currently indisposed.
-Faraday?!

18:48.189 --> 18:50.608
I trust the job is going well?

18:50.692 --> 18:53.111
Fuck you, put Lucy back on!

18:53.695 --> 18:58.449
This chairjock bitch should feel grateful
to be kissing the ground.

18:58.533 --> 19:02.912
I was worried I might've
overscrambled her brain.

19:02.996 --> 19:05.206
Take your fucking foot off her!

19:05.290 --> 19:08.626
Don't be so serious.
I'm just having a ball of a time.

19:08.710 --> 19:13.131
Besides, I won't have to lift a finger
when Arasaka's done with her.

19:13.214 --> 19:14.883
Faraday!

19:16.467 --> 19:18.386
You're rapidly degenerating!

19:18.469 --> 19:21.222
At this rate, you're gonna
go psycho in seconds!

19:21.306 --> 19:25.852
Elite Militech forces are closing in.

19:25.935 --> 19:30.231
Install the soft, use the cyberskeleton,
David. Lead your crew to safety.

19:30.315 --> 19:36.237
Personally, I think it's beyond you.
Clearly Arasaka sees something I don't.

19:36.821 --> 19:43.036
If you're truly so special, boy,
show me what you can do. Survive.

19:45.330 --> 19:49.375
I'll kill him! I'm gonna go kill him!

19:50.210 --> 19:53.379
I'll kill him! I'll kill him…

19:53.963 --> 19:56.007
I'm gonna fucking--

19:59.093 --> 20:00.470
You okay?

20:00.553 --> 20:02.138
I'm gonna go save Lucy.

20:02.222 --> 20:05.433
Uhh… Nope, I think your brain's fried.

20:05.516 --> 20:09.520
Faraday's double-crossed us.
He's got Lucy.

20:09.604 --> 20:11.439
Huh? What do you mean?

20:11.522 --> 20:14.609
That fucker.
I'm gonna fucking put him in the ground!

20:14.692 --> 20:16.736
I swear, he's gonna fucking die…

20:16.819 --> 20:17.654
David…

20:19.572 --> 20:21.241
Falco! What happened?

20:21.324 --> 20:22.951
Kiwi got me.

20:23.034 --> 20:23.910
What?!

20:23.993 --> 20:26.204
She led us into a trap.

20:26.287 --> 20:29.249
Oh, that hag. She's in it too?

20:29.332 --> 20:31.501
She's a fucking flatline
when I see her next!

20:37.924 --> 20:39.425
Here we go again!

20:41.719 --> 20:42.887
Shit!

20:42.971 --> 20:45.139
Militech's really out to kill us!

20:45.807 --> 20:49.018
I've never seen anything like this.

20:49.102 --> 20:51.312
How can anyone walk with this on?

20:51.396 --> 20:56.150
Two compact thrusters're built in.
Same kind you get on an AV.

20:56.234 --> 21:00.989
On top of that, Arasaka engineered in
a gravity modification prototype.

21:03.700 --> 21:08.371
It can generate unidirectional
grav fields, magnetic forces, too…

21:09.038 --> 21:11.124
That's the magnetic force generator?

21:16.004 --> 21:19.132
Hot damn!
He just mowed a small squad down!

21:19.215 --> 21:22.468
He's using his Sandevistan, too.

21:44.907 --> 21:46.075
He's flying!

21:46.159 --> 21:47.827
That's the gravitational field?

21:54.334 --> 21:56.544
But this tech hasn't left
its testing stage.

21:57.337 --> 21:59.172
The controls are too complex.

21:59.255 --> 22:03.843
There's no guarantee that the equipper's
nerves will be able to withstand it.

22:03.926 --> 22:07.638
It requires an insane level
of mental fortitude against implants.

22:07.722 --> 22:10.641
A one-way ticket to
cyberpsychosis, you mean.

22:22.362 --> 22:23.905
They got him?!

22:24.530 --> 22:25.907
David…

22:34.373 --> 22:35.666
He's still going!

22:35.750 --> 22:38.002
His body is, but…

22:38.086 --> 22:43.341
The more he uses it, the closer he will be
to overloading his cyberware capacity.

22:43.424 --> 22:48.221
But in exchange, the short-term
power it generates is…

22:52.016 --> 22:55.436
unlike anything devised
on this side of sanity.

23:05.029 --> 23:06.280
David?

23:12.328 --> 23:15.498
We're going after Faraday
for betraying us.

23:15.581 --> 23:17.333
And we're gonna save Lucy.

23:17.959 --> 23:19.043
You say that but…

23:19.127 --> 23:21.003
Equal share of the pot.

23:22.213 --> 23:24.465
That's my style.

23:27.009 --> 23:28.886
Alright, buddy.

23:29.679 --> 23:31.722
Onwards to hell.
